穿云 core muse.19: DNS query view for the app.
The DNS client reports every answer it hands out (network exchange, cache hit,
optimistic cache, rejected, failed) to one process-wide hook: domain, type, the
server that answered (inside a group: the member, noted by the group transport),
its configured address, answers, rcode, elapsed time, cached. The hook is nil
unless the local API has a subscriber, so with nobody watching the cost is one
atomic load per query. The local API serves it at /dns/queries (websocket:
buffered 500-entry ring first, then live batches; plain GET = snapshot; DELETE
clears). The first websocket installs the hook and the last one removes it; no
timer or polling. Standard DNS behaviour is unchanged.

